# The character and the suit both arms of the quality-immunity check share.
# Included by quality-self-immune-plain.keys and quality-self-immune-quality.keys.
# Read by tools/check_quality_self_immune.sh (bd inc-to9x).
#
# WHY THE DAMAGE MUST COME FROM A MONSTER. Only one route brings an elemental
# damage type to a WORN suit: the equipment block in Magic::Blast
# (src/Effects.cpp:378-403), which damages one carried item when a blast that
# ALLOWED a save was not saved against. Three conditions gate it, and the third
# is why no self-inflicted blast can be used:
#   - EF_PARTIAL on the effect, or Magic::Blast never rolls a save and
#     save_type stays NOSAVE. The "Breath Weapon" resource (lib/main.irc:193)
#     carries `sval: REF partial`, which is that flag.
#   - the save must FAIL, because e.Resist is what the block tests.
#   - the blast's actor must not be the item's owner. src/Item.cpp:1470 reads
#     "If you are attacking your own items, ignore their hardness" and sets
#     hard = 0, which erases the -1 immunity sentinel along with every other
#     hardness. ThrowDmg clears isTrap and eID on the way in, so for the
#     equipment block that test is just EActor == owner: a character who
#     fireballs himself, or steps on his own trap, measures nothing. Both were
#     tried and both showed "vs. 0 (leather)" on a suit whose own page said it
#     was immune.
#
# The wearer must also have NO resistance to the damage type. Creature::Damage
# sets e.Resist for ANY non-weapon damage the victim resists at all
# (src/Fight.cpp:6292 and :6318), so one point of fire resistance makes the
# block skip the wearer's gear entirely. That is why the suit stays +0 while it
# burns: the quality's EA_GRANT is PLUS_3PER1 of the item's plus, so at +0 it
# gives the wearer nothing and the item half stays measurable. Arm B buys the
# plus back with two scrolls AFTER the burning, and measures the wearer half
# there.
#
# WHY A MAGE AT LEVEL FIVE. Nothing here casts a spell; the four levels are hit
# points and nothing else. Three hell hounds bite and breathe at him for a
# hundred turns, and a level-one character spends that whole time in the Cheat
# Death prompt. His Reflex save stays poor, which is what the measurement
# wants: a MADE save sets e.Resist, and the equipment block runs only when
# e.Resist is false.
#
# WHY A PLAIN LEATHER SUIT. MaterialHardness gives MAT_LEATHER a fire hardness
# of 0 (src/Item.cpp:1241), so every roll that reaches it scratches it, and
# Item::Damage names the material in its own numbers line -- "vs. 0 (leather)"
# against "vs. Immune (leather)" is the whole measurement.

@include chargen-mage.keys

# chargen-mage.keys stops on the arrival room description. Dismiss it, or the
# [w] below is eaten by the description.
ESC

# Wizard switches, counted from the top of the list in src/Tables.cpp:2679:
#   1 Cheat Death, 3 Free Advancement, 5 Always Rest Safely.
# Cheat Death is not a convenience: an unanswered death prompt spends every key
# after it. Always Rest Safely stops new monsters being generated while the
# character stands still, which is what keeps the room to the three summoned
# hounds for most of the hundred turns. Freeze Monsters is NOT set and must not be: a breath is
# the hound's own turn, not an answer to a blow.
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
SPACE
DOWN*2
SPACE
DOWN*2
SPACE
ESC
@until "Things in View" ESC

# Four free levels, for hit points. 'd' opens the character screen and 'G'
# gains a level; SPACE leaves it.
d
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic Feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic Feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic Feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic Feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
SPACE
@until "Things in View" ESC

# --- the suit whose hit points are measured -----------------------------
# Column 15 of the acquisition prompt is Armours. The list shows the selected
# row and the row under it, so @until stops with "Leather armour" one row below
# the cursor and the extra DOWN selects it. No "Enter Item Level" prompt
# follows, because a plain leather suit has no inherent plus.
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*15
@until "Leather armour" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
j
SPACE
@while "two-handed" y
# The mage's armour slot was empty, so the swap put nothing in the air. Empty
# the weapon hand instead and stow the knife: with SL_WEAPON empty, the
# equipment block reaches the armour on one coin toss rather than two
# (src/Effects.cpp:384-387).
b
SPACE
s
@until "Things in View" ESC

# An unidentified item's page hides its hit points, and the hit points are half
# the measurement.
w
@choose "Identify Whole Pack"
@until "Things in View" ESC
